{
  time = "2026-09-07T11:40:45+00:00";
  condition = config.programs.claude-code.enable;
  message = ''
    The `settings.json` generated by `programs.claude-code` (from
    `settings`, `marketplaces`, or `mcpServers`) is now installed as a
    real, writable file instead of a symlink into the Nix store. Claude
    Code's own background worker periodically unlinks this file as part
    of its file management; for a symlink into the read-only store this
    silently deleted every user-configured setting until the next
    `home-manager switch` recreated it, at which point the same worker
    deleted it again.

    The file is still fully regenerated on every `home-manager switch`, so
    any in-app edit to `settings.json` will only survive until the next
    switch, the same as any other Home Manager managed file.
  '';
}
